{title: 241 - Jesus, the Very Thought of Thee}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #241 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 241}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Jesus, the [Am/C]very thought [D]of [G]Thee
[D7/A]With [G]sweetness [Em]fills [Am]the breast;
[Am]But sweeter [D]far Thy [Bm]face [C]to see,
[G/D]And in [D7]Thy presence [G]rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]No voice can [Am/C]sing, [Bm]no [Am]heart [D]can [G]frame,
[D7/A]Nor [G]can [D/F#]the [G]memory [Am]find
[Am]A sweeter [D]sound than [Bm]Jesus' [C/E]name,
[G/D]The Savior [D7]of [G]mankind.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]O hope of every [Am]contrite [G]heart!
[D7/A]O [G]joy of [Em]all [Am]the meek,
[Am]to those [D]who fall, how [Bm]kind [C]thou art!
[G/D]How good [D7]to those [G]who seek!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]But what to [Am/C]those [Bm]who [Am]find? [D]Ah, [G]this
[D7/A]nor [G]tongue nor [Em]pen [Am]can show;
[Am]the love [D]of Jesus, [Bm]what [C]it is,
[G/D]none but his [D7]loved ones [G]know.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[G]Jesus, our [Am/C]only joy [D]be [G]thou,
[D7/A]as [G]thou our [Em]prize [Am]wilt be;
[Am]Jesus, [D]be thou our [Bm]glory [C/E]now,
[G/D]and through [D7]eternity.
{end_of_verse}
